Z||000000||beachbomb||12-28-2000||04:27 PM||||Hi all, i recently aquired a second indy pace car for parts, after having it a couple weeks i have noticed differences between this Indy and my drivable Indy, they are:<BR>1. While looking at the engine, the dipstick on the second Indy comes up between the exhaust manifold, on my drivable Indy it comes up by the thermostat housing<BR>2. Second Indy does not have heat shields near the water pump or near the exhaust manifold, drivable Indy does.<BR>Both of these differences look to be factory made, not someone just moving around items.<BR>Are these differences the recalls that where done? I'm thinking the recalls where not done on my second Indy but i'm not sure, anyone that might know, plmk. Thnaks alot..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||turbo86se||12-28-2000||10:32 PM||||Can't help you with the above, Jim, but remember that other Indy I told you about? Well, the other day on my way back from MD I found it!!<P>It is sweet! Body in excellent shape, and the interior is MINT! 4-spd, all options. Seats and carpet are excellent. One headlight stuck up, tires dry-rotted, spoiler stantions cracked, paint real good, couldn't see the engine. It even had stickers that said "Indy Fiero" on the bottom of the doors. It's been sitting in the same place for at least three years, I'll call tomorrow and find out more. <P>oh yeah, 80K miles<p>[This message has been edited by turbo86se (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||10
